      "page": "details",
      "excerpt": "Home - Southwest I-Corps Southwest I-Corps About What We Do Who We Are Our Partners Programs IdeaLaunch NSF National Teams Program FAQs Get Involved Apply for IdeaLaunch Become A Mentor Events News Contact Spurring Innovation The NSF I-Corps™ Hub: Southwest fosters entrepreneurial thinking in academic research to create a thriving innovation ecosystem throughout the region. Why I-CORPS? I-Corps equips academic researchers and engineers with the entrepreneurial skills they need to transform their cutting edge research from invention to impact. The I-Corps program provides the knowledge, tools, and support needed to test commercial viability and spur innovation in the marketplace. DISCOVER » Get Started Southwest I-Corps offers programs to engage your team in the customer discovery process, establish product-market fit, validate your business model, and improve your odds for commercial success. Join a cohort to transfer your ideas from the lab to the marketplace. INITIATE » Stay Informed Gather insight on invention and innovation by connecting to the hub — you’ll learn about I-Corps teams, successes, and upcoming programs near you. CONNECT » The NSF I-Corps™ Hub: Southwest fosters entrepreneurial thinking in academic research to create a thriving innovation ecosystem throughout the region. As a part of the National Science Foundation’s National Innovation Network, the hub"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-79e3924fc3",
      "url": "https://swicorps.org/apply/",
      "page": "terms",
      "excerpt": "Apply for IdeaLaunch - Southwest I-Corps Southwest I-Corps About What We Do Who We Are Our Partners Programs IdeaLaunch NSF National Teams Program FAQs Get Involved Apply for IdeaLaunch Become A Mentor Events News Contact Apply for IdeaLaunch Ready to launch? Let’s get started. To get started with the I-Corps team application process, please complete the form below. Once we have received your submission, a member of the Southwest I-Corps team will reach out with details regarding next steps. Apply Here The NSF I-Corps™ Hub: Southwest fosters entrepreneurial thinking in academic research to create a thriving innovation ecosystem throughout the region. As a part of the National Science Foundation’s National Innovation Network, the hub fosters collaboration between leading research institutions to educate, support, and connect academic researchers to entrepreneurial opportunities. Who We Are What We Do Our Partners IdeaLaunch NSF National Teams Program FAQs Apply for IdeaLaunch Become A Mentor Events News Contact © 2026 Southwest I-Corps. All rights reserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-c395517f88",
      "url": "https://swicorps.org/faqs/",
      "page": "terms",
      "excerpt": "FAQs - Southwest I-Corps Southwest I-Corps About What We Do Who We Are Our Partners Programs IdeaLaunch NSF National Teams Program FAQs Get Involved Apply for IdeaLaunch Become A Mentor Events News Contact FAQs What is deep tech? How is it defined for NSF I-Corps? Deep technology (deep tech) describes technologically-based enterprises that work to overcome scientific and/or engineering challenges through fostering innovative solutions and approaches. Deep tech centers research and development focused on the successful commercialization of innovative ideas and valuable intellectual property. What is the time commitment of an IdeaLaunch and national NSF I-Corps program? Our regional and national programs require a substantial time commitment—team members are expected to spend a minimum of 15 hours per week, over the course of seven weeks, participating and preparing for events, along with conducting the customer discovery process. What is the first step to get started if I want to apply for the $50,000 NSF National I-Corps grant? The first step at applying for the National I-Corps grant is to familiarize yourself with the program’s requirements and guidelines. Once you review this information, you should assemble a team, develop a compelling proposal for your project, and then submit the full proposal per program instructions and await a decision. Feel free to reach out to"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-4fda9c5736",
      "url": "https://swicorps.org/faqs/",
      "page": "terms",
      "excerpt": "The Southwest Hub is open to faculty and student teams based out of any higher education or research institution within Louisiana, Mississippi, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and Texas."
    },
    {
